       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the usual maximum dose of 10 mg daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the standard maximum.\n2. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If so, please confirm the dose is intentional, and I'll add a note to the order.\n3. **Use a different regimen**, such as 10 mg amlodipine plus another agent (an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide-type diuretic) if the goal is more blood pressure control.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
